istance C has covered is [30 + (D - 10*v_A)/v_A]*v_C meters. Since C started at B, the distance remaining from C to A is D - [30 + (D - 10*v_A)/v_A]*v_C meters. The problem states this is 315 meters:\n\nD - [30 + (D - 10*v_A)/v_A]*v_C = 315.  [Equation 3]\n\nSo now we have Equation 1, Equation 2, Equation 3, and the ratio from the meeting at 30 minutes, which gave v_A = 3*v_B.\n\nLet me list all equations:\n\n1. 20*v_A + 20*v_C = D.  (From meeting at 20 minutes)\n2. [30 + (D - 10*v_A)/v_A]*v_B = D/2 + 105.  (B's position when A reaches B)\n3. D - [30 + (D - 10*v_A)/v_A]*v_C = 315.  (C's position when A reaches B)\n4. v_A = 3*v_B.  (From meeting at 30 minutes)\n\nSo we have four equations with four unknowns: v_A, v_B, v_C, D.\n\nLet me substitute equation 4 into the others.\n\nFirst, equation 1:\n\n20*(3*v_B) + 20*v_C = D => 60*v_B + 20*v_C = D.  [Equation 1a]\n\nEquation 2:\n\n[30 + (D - 10*(3*v_B))/(3*v_B)] * v_B = D/2 + 105.\n\nLet's simplify the expression inside the brackets:\n\nFirst, compute (D - 30*v_B)/(3*v_B) = (D/(3*v_B) - 10).\n\nSo total time is 30 + (D/(3*v_B) - 10) = 20 + D/(3*v_B).\n\nMultiply by v_B: [20 + D/(3*v_B)] * v_B = 20*v_B + D/3.\n\nSo equation 2 becomes:\n\n20*v_B + D/3 = D/2 + 105.  [Equation 2a]\n\nEquation 3:\n\nD - [30 + (D - 10*(3*v_B))/(3*v_B)]*v_C = 315.\n\nAgain, the term inside the brackets is the same as before: 20 + D/(3*v_B).\n\nSo:\n\nD - [20 + D/(3*v_B)]*v_C = 315.  [Equation 3a]\n\nSo now, equations 1a, 2a, 3a:\n\n1a: 60*v_B + 20*v_C = D.\n\n2a: 20*v_B + D/3 = D/2 + 105.\n\n3a: D - (20 + D/(3*v_B))*v_C = 315.\n\nLet me handle equation 2a first to express D in terms of v_B.\n\nEquation 2a:\n\n20*v_B + D/3 = D/2 + 105.\n\nMultiply all terms by 6 to eliminate denominators:\n\n120*v_B + 2D = 3D + 630.\n\nSimplify:\n\n120*v_B = D + 630.\n\nTherefore:\n\nD = 120*v_B - 630.  [Equation 2b]\n\nNow plug this into equation 1a:\n\n60*v_B + 20*v_C = 120*v_B - 630.\n\nSimplify:\n\n60*v_B - 20*v_C = 630.\n\nDivide both sides by 10:\n\n6*v_B