ble=60 +53 +392=505.\n\nNot234.\n\nBut the probability needed is13/200=234/3600. Therefore, the total favorable pairs must be234. Therefore, only for certainx do the total pairs equal234.\n\nBut from above, forx=12, the total is235, which is close. Maybe there's a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps whenK +8 is not a divisor of120, meaning case2 contributes0, and case1 + case3=60 + case3=234. Therefore, case3=174. Let's check:\n\nIf case3=174, then:\n\n174= (60 -D)*D + D(D -1)/2.\n\nWe need to solve forD:\n\n174=60D -D\u00b2 + (D\u00b2 -D)/2=60D -D\u00b2 +0.5D\u00b2 -0.5D=60D -0.5D\u00b2 -0.5D=59.5D -0.5D\u00b2\n\nMultiply by2:\n\n348=119D -D\u00b2\n\n=>D\u00b2 -119D +348=0\n\nSolve quadratic equation:\n\nD=(119 \u00b1\u221a(119\u00b2 -4*1*348))/2= (119 \u00b1\u221a(14161 -1392))/2= (119 \u00b1\u221a12769)/2= (119 \u00b1113)/2\n\nSoD=(119 +113)/2=232/2=116 orD=(119 -113)/2=6/2=3\n\nD=3. SinceD=116 is impossible (maxD=15).\n\nSoD=3.\n\nTherefore, case3 pairs=174 impliesD=3.\n\nSoD= floor(120/x -8)=3.\n\nTherefore:\n\n3 <=120/x -8 <4\n\n=>11 <=120/x <12\n\n=>120/12 <x <=120/11\n\n=>10 <x <=120/11\u224810.909...\n\nTherefore,x must be in(10,10.909...].\n\nButx must be such thatD=3. Also, sincex is not necessarily an integer, butD must be integer.\n\nThus, the range ofx is10 <x <=120/11\u224810.909...\n\nBut we need to check if forx in this range, case3=174.\n\nBut how does this relate to the probability?\n\nIf case2 contributes0 (since120/x -8 is not integer), then total favorable= case1 + case3=60 +174=234.\n\nTherefore, the probability=234/3600=13/200.\n\nTherefore, this occurs when case2=0, which happens when120/x -8 is not integer, and case3=174, which happens whenD=3.\n\nThus, the condition is:\n\n3 <=120/x -8 <4\n\n=>11 <=120/x <12\n\n=>120/12 <x <=120/11\n\n=>10 <x <=approximately10.909.\n\nButx must be a real number in this interval.\n\nTherefore, the range ofx is10 <x <=120/11 km/h.\n\nBut120/11\u224810.909090...\n\nThus, the range isx such that10 <x <=120/11.\